Annotations: |
  This cell is the presentation-agnostic value-type model for the browser's address/navigation
  toolbars: what a single toolbar control looks like (`ToolbarElement`), what its overflow-menu
  entries look like (`ToolbarMenuElement`), what a loading/spinner state looks like
  (`LoadingConfig`), and the shared border-display policy the toolbar UI applies
  (`ToolbarManager`). Concrete button rendering (an internal button-view-subclass hierarchy and
  its address/navigation-bar compositions) lives deeper in this target and is out of scope for
  this cell; this cell documents only the public contract those internals render.

---

"ToolbarManager()":
  location: ToolbarManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Policy for which border (top/bottom/none) a toolbar should draw, based on toolbar position,
    private-browsing state, and scroll offset.
  methods:
    "getAddressBorderPosition(for toolbarPosition: AddressToolbarPosition, isPrivate: Bool, scrollY: CGFloat) -> position:AddressToolbarBorderPosition": |
      Decide which border the address toolbar should draw right now.

      `toolbarPosition`: whether the address toolbar is docked at the top or bottom of the screen
      `isPrivate`: whether the current tab is a private-browsing tab
      `scrollY`: current vertical scroll offset of the active web page
      `position`: the border to draw, if any
    "shouldDisplayNavigationBorder(toolbarPosition: AddressToolbarPosition) -> shouldDisplay:Bool": |
      Whether the navigation (bottom) toolbar should draw a top border.

      `toolbarPosition`: whether the address toolbar is docked at the top or bottom of the screen

"ToolbarManager::DefaultToolbarManager()":
  location: ToolbarManager.swift
  annotations: |
    The concrete, stateless border policy described above: bottom-docked address toolbars always
    get a top border; top-docked ones get a bottom border only when scrolled or in private mode.

"AddressToolbarBorderConfiguration(a11yIdentifier: String, borderPosition: AddressToolbarBorderPosition?)":
  location: ToolbarManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Pairs an accessibility identifier with the border position resolved by `ToolbarManager`, for
    the view layer to apply.

    `a11yIdentifier`: accessibility identifier of the border view to configure
    `borderPosition`: the border position to display, or nil for no border

"ToolbarElement()":
  location: ToolbarElement.swift
  annotations: |
    Full visual/interaction state of one toolbar control (back button, tab counter, menu button,
    etc.), independent of how it is rendered. Equatable so the rendering layer can skip
    reconfiguring a button whose element hasn't changed.
  properties:
    "iconName -> String?": |
      Name of the icon image to display, if any.
    "title -> String?": |
      Text title to display instead of/alongside an icon.
    "badgeImageName -> String?": |
      Name of a small badge image overlaid on the control (e.g. a tracking-protection warning).
    "loadingConfig -> LoadingConfig?": |
      When present, the control renders a loading spinner instead of its normal icon.
    "numberOfTabs -> Int?": |
      When present, the control is a tab-count button and displays this count.
    "isEnabled -> Bool": |
      Whether the control can be interacted with.
    "isSelected -> Bool": |
      Whether the control should render as highlighted/selected.
    "a11yLabel -> String": |
      Accessibility label of the control.
    "a11yId -> String": |
      Accessibility identifier of the control.
    "cacheId -> String?": |
      Stable key used to reuse the same underlying button instance across visual state changes;
      falls back to the control's accessibility identifier when absent.
    "onSelected -> ((UIButton) -> Void)?": |
      Closure invoked when the control is tapped.
    "onLongPress -> ((UIButton) -> Void)?": |
      Closure invoked when the control is long-pressed.
    "menuElements -> [ToolbarMenuElement]": |
      Overflow-menu entries shown when the control is pressed, if any.

      Also carries additional presentation flags not itemized individually here (RTL image
      flipping, custom/highlighted color overrides, large-content-viewer title, bottom/mask
      badge images, and the two tab-transition screenshots used by the stacked-tab button) that
      together fully describe the control's rendered appearance.

"ToolbarMenuElement(title: String, imageName: String?, a11yIdentifier: String?, onSelected: SelectionHandler?)":
  location: ToolbarMenuElement.swift
  annotations: |
    One entry in a toolbar control's overflow menu.

    `title`: menu entry title
    `imageName`: optional icon image name for the entry
    `a11yIdentifier`: accessibility identifier of the entry
    `onSelected`: a no-return closure, taking the pressed button, invoked when the entry is
    selected

"LoadingConfig(isLoading: Bool, a11yLabel: String)":
  location: LoadingConfig.swift
  annotations: |
    Marks a `ToolbarElement` as showing a loading spinner instead of its normal icon.

    `isLoading`: whether the loading spinner should currently be shown
    `a11yLabel`: accessibility label announced while loading
  properties:
    "isLoading -> Bool": |
      Whether the loading spinner should currently be shown.

